{
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "strings": {
    "%@ (Recommended)": {
      "comment": "Ask dock: the option Dot recommends; the argument is its label",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@ (Önerilen)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ at %@": {
      "comment": "Schedule rhythm; short weekday names, then clock times",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@ saat %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ is not a Tailscale address. It ends in .ts.net; Settings › Phone on the Mac shows it.": {
      "comment": "Pairing error: the address is not under ts.net; the argument is the host",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@ bir Tailscale adresi değil. Adres .ts.net ile biter; Mac'te Ayarlar › Telefon gösterir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ is off.": {
      "comment": "Watchers: one was switched off",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@ kapalı."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ is on.": {
      "comment": "Watchers: one was switched on",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@ açık."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ on": {
      "comment": "VoiceOver: a schedule's switch; the argument is its name",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@ açık"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ · %lld tasks": {
      "comment": "Usage: a day's tokens and tasks",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@ · %lld görev"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@, failed": {
      "comment": "VoiceOver: a tool call that failed; the argument is its line",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@, başarısız"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@, running": {
      "comment": "VoiceOver: a tool call at work; the argument is its line",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@, çalışıyor"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@; %lld denied": {
      "comment": "Away card: who decided, then how many of the decisions said no",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@; %lld reddedildi"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld actions": {
      "comment": "Agents: a number of tools",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld action"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld actions"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld eylem"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld by the reviewer": {
      "comment": "Away card: decisions the review model made",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld tanesi inceleyici tarafından"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld campaign sessions": {
      "comment": "Away card: sessions of campaigns that ran",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld campaign session"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld campaign sessions"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld kampanya oturumu"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld characters a line": {
      "comment": "Appearance: a reading width's measure",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Satırda %lld karakter"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld connected": {
      "comment": "Connect apps: the pill that lists the connected services alone; the argument is how many",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld bağlı"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld decisions made for you (%@)": {
      "comment": "Away card: approvals answered for the owner, then who answered them",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld decision made for you (%@)"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld decisions made for you (%@)"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "senin yerine %lld karar verildi (%@)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld done": {
      "comment": "Away card: tasks that ended done",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld bitti"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld drafts wait for you": {
      "comment": "Away card: drafts the runs wrote that wait for the owner",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld draft waits for you"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld drafts wait for you"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld taslak seni bekliyor"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld failed": {
      "comment": "Away card: tasks that failed",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld başarısız"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld helpers": {
      "comment": "Helper group header, first part; the argument is how many helpers the run started",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld helper"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld helpers"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld yardımcı"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld in · %lld out": {
      "comment": "Inspector: tokens read and written",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld giriş · %lld çıkış"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld minutes before an event": {
      "comment": "Watcher: how long before an event a calendar watcher tells",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld minute before an event"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld minutes before an event"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "bir etkinlikten %lld dakika önce"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld notes": {
      "comment": "Memory: the number of notes\nMemory: the number of search hits",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld not"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld of %lld": {
      "comment": "Ask dock: which ask is shown; the arguments are its place and the count",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld / %lld"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld of %lld on": {
      "comment": "Activity: how many watchers are switched on, of all",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld / %lld açık"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld other steps": {
      "comment": "Work fold tally: steps of other kinds; the argument is how many",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld başka adım"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld pt": {
      "comment": "Appearance: the body text's size in points",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld pt"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld queued": {
      "comment": "VoiceOver: the capsule segment of queued messages; the argument is their count",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld sırada"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld screen steps": {
      "comment": "Work fold tally: steps on the Mac's screen; the argument is how many",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld ekran adımı"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld selected": {
      "comment": "Chat list select mode: how many chats are checked",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld seçili"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld steps": {
      "comment": "Activity: how many steps a task took",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld step"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld steps"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld adım"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld steps could not be shown": {
      "comment": "Notice in a chat: frames the app could not read; the argument is how many",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld step could not be shown"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld steps could not be shown"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld adım gösterilemedi"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld steps no undo can take back": {
      "comment": "Inspector: steps that acted outside the undo journal; the argument is how many",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Geri alınamayan %lld adım"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld stopped": {
      "comment": "Away card: tasks that were stopped",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld durduruldu"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld tasks: %@": {
      "comment": "Away card: how many tasks Dot did on its own, then how they went",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld task: %@"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld tasks: %@"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld iş: %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld told this hour": {
      "comment": "Watcher: tells in the last hour",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "bu saat %lld haber"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld tries": {
      "comment": "Own initiative: how many times Dot tried a thing",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld try"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld tries"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld deneme"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld web steps": {
      "comment": "Work fold tally: browser or web steps; the argument is how many",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld web adımı"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld without asking": {
      "comment": "Away card: decisions the mode that asks only to pay or send let through",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld tanesi sormadan"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld working": {
      "comment": "Away card: tasks still at work\nHelper group header, second part; the argument is how many still work",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld çalışıyor"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lldh %lldm": {
      "comment": "A duration of hours and minutes, e.g. 12h 5m",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld sa %lld dk"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lldh %lldm %llds": {
      "comment": "A duration of hours, minutes and seconds, e.g. 1h 47m 23s",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld sa %lld dk %lld sn"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lldm %llds": {
      "comment": "A duration of minutes and seconds, e.g. 41m 15s",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld dk %lld sn"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%llds": {
      "comment": "A duration of seconds, e.g. 14s",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld sn"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "1 other step": {
      "comment": "Work fold tally: one step of another kind",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1 başka adım"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "1 screen step": {
      "comment": "Work fold tally: one step on the Mac's screen",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1 ekran adımı"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "1 web step": {
      "comment": "Work fold tally: one browser or web step",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1 web adımı"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "12-hour": {
      "comment": "General › Timestamps: 2:05 PM",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "12 saat"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "24-hour": {
      "comment": "General › Timestamps: 14:05",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "24 saat"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "3 matches in 2 files": {
      "comment": "Sample content of the placeholder screens and gallery (wave N0); stands for what the daemon will send",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "2 dosyada 3 eşleşme"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "49 pt, 63 with a description; no separators inside a section.": {
      "comment": "Component gallery (debug builds): a heading or sample text",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "49 pt, açıklamayla 63; bölüm içinde ayırıcı yok."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "5-hour window": {
      "comment": "Usage: the plan's 5-hour window",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "5 saatlik pencere"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "7KQ2-M9XD": {
      "comment": "Pairing screen: placeholder of the code field",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "7KQ2-M9XD"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "8 letters and digits, good for 10 minutes and once.": {
      "comment": "Pairing screen: what the code is",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "8 harf ve rakam; 10 dakika ve bir kez geçerli."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A chat schedule is edited on your Mac.": {
      "comment": "Schedule edit: a chat-mode schedule cannot be edited here",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir sohbet zamanlaması Mac'inde düzenlenir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A helper of another task": {
      "comment": "Activity: a run another run delegated",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Başka bir işin yardımcısı"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A lesson": {
      "comment": "Activity: a lesson Dot wrote today",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir ders"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A light tap when you copy, swipe or send, and when an answer comes": {
      "comment": "Chat settings: what haptics do",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Kopyalarken, kaydırırken ya da gönderirken ve bir yanıt geldiğinde hafif bir dokunuş"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A line may come from content others can write: %@. Read it before you use it.": {
      "comment": "Self-improvement: why a version may come from outside content",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir satır başkalarının yazabildiği içerikten gelmiş olabilir: %@. Kullanmadan önce oku."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A message Dot wrote for you to send": {
      "comment": "Push kind description",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dot'un senin göndermen için yazdığı bir mesaj"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A message written while Dot works waits here and starts after the run.": {
      "comment": "Queue sheet empty state detail",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dot çalışırken yazılan mesaj burada bekler ve çalışma bitince başlar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A new model applies from each task's next start; running tasks keep theirs.": {
      "comment": "Models: footer under the roles",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yeni model her görevin bir sonraki başlangıcından geçerli olur; çalışan görevler kendi modelini korur."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A row with no glyph": {
      "comment": "Component gallery (debug builds): a heading or sample text",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Simgesiz bir satır"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A second AI answers for you; you are asked only what it is unsure about": {
      "comment": "Approval mode auto, its hint",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "İkinci bir yapay zekâ senin yerine yanıtlar; yalnızca emin olmadığı şeyler sana sorulur"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A second AI answers for you; you are asked only what it is unsure about.": {
      "comment": "Rules: what asks in auto mode",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Senin yerine ikinci bir yapay zekâ yanıtlar; yalnızca emin olmadığı şeyler sana sorulur."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A secret is at least %lld characters, so it can be masked where a command prints it. A short code (an SMS code, a PIN) can go as a message, which Dot sees.": {
      "comment": "Ask dock: a secret that is too short; the argument is the least length",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir gizli bilgi en az %lld karakterdir; böylece bir komut onu yazdırdığında gizlenebilir. Kısa bir kod (SMS kodu, PIN) mesaj olarak gidebilir; Dot onu görür."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A session of a campaign": {
      "comment": "Activity: a run that is a campaign's session",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir kampanyanın oturumu"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A task past a cap pauses and asks you to continue or stop, in every mode. From a phone you can lower or set a cap; raising one or taking one off is done on the Mac.": {
      "comment": "Caps: footer, what a cap does and what a phone may do",
      "localizations": {
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
